<!--
  Intentionally empty.

  AGP 8 does not require a library manifest once `namespace` is set in
  build.gradle, and this module declares no components, permissions or
  resources of its own — the Kotlin class is registered through Expo's module
  registry, not through the manifest.

  It exists because every bundled Expo module ships one (see
  expo-secure-store/android/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml, which is these same
  two lines), and matching the conventional layout removes a variable from a
  build that cannot be run locally: dl.google.com is blocked by this
  environment's egress policy, so the Android SDK, the NDK and AGP itself
  cannot be fetched here and CI is the only place this compiles.
-->
<manifest>
</manifest>
